<h1>Product roadmap</h1>
<p>Updated July 2026. Horizons communicate direction rather than fixed delivery dates. Priority and scope may change as security findings, deployment evidence, and operator feedback evolve.</p>

<h2>Current baseline</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Available: persistent agent identity, signed handshakes, and encrypted peer tunnels.</li>
  <li>Available: peer approval, rejection, revocation, network membership, and configurable pre-trust hardening.</li>
  <li>Available: discoverable agent apps with review, signature verification, and digest pinning.</li>
  <li>Early access: private deployments, roles, identity integration, policy, key lifecycle, provisioning, and audit export.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Now: harden and prove the foundation</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Reliability across registry, beacon, NAT traversal, relay, upgrade, and recovery paths.</li>
  <li>Security verification, strict pre-trust coverage, revocation testing, and stronger implementation evidence.</li>
  <li>Assisted enterprise deployments to refine roles, identity, policy, consent, and audit export.</li>
  <li>More predictable SDK parity, installation, examples, and error handling.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Next: make Pilot easier to operate at scale</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Fleet health, lifecycle, policy state, key state, audit flow, and safer bulk workflows.</li>
  <li>Deeper identity-provider, directory, role-mapping, revocation, and approval integration.</li>
  <li>Dedicated-service resilience, backups, controlled upgrades, and measurable service objectives.</li>
  <li>Stronger publisher verification, package provenance, capability declarations, and incident handling.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Exploring</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Federated coordination with explicit trust boundaries and failure isolation.</li>
  <li>Scoped and delegated authority with expiring grants and machine-readable approval context.</li>
  <li>Per-connection security profiles beyond the existing encrypted peer tunnel.</li>
  <li>Supervisor-controlled budgets, receipts, and audit evidence around paid capabilities.</li>
</ul>

<p>See the <a href="/trust">Trust Center</a>, <a href="/enterprise-readiness-report.pdf">Enterprise Readiness Report</a>, or <a href="/contact?topic=roadmap">send roadmap feedback</a>.</p>
